msgid "Using Hibernate ORM and Jakarta Persistence"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate ORM is the de facto standard Jakarta Persistence (formerly known "
"as JPA) implementation and offers you the full breadth of an Object "
"Relational Mapper.\n"
"It works beautifully in Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Solution"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend that you follow the instructions in the next sections and "
"create the application step by step.\n"
"However, you can go right to the completed example."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Clone the Git repository: `git clone {quickstarts-clone-url}`, or download "
"an {quickstarts-archive-url}[archive]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The solution is located in the `hibernate-orm-quickstart` link:{quickstarts-"
"tree-url}/hibernate-orm-quickstart[directory]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting up and configuring Hibernate ORM"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When using Hibernate ORM in Quarkus, you don't need to have a `persistence."
"xml` resource to configure it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using such a classic configuration file is an option, but unnecessary unless "
"you have specific advanced needs;\n"
"so we'll see first how Hibernate ORM can be configured without a "
"`persistence.xml` resource."
msgstr ""

msgid "In Quarkus, you only need to:"
msgstr ""

msgid "add your configuration settings in `{config-file}`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"annotate your entities with `@Entity` and any other mapping annotation as "
"usual"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Other configuration needs have been automated: Quarkus will make some "
"opinionated choices and educated guesses."
msgstr ""

msgid "Add the following dependencies to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid "the Hibernate ORM extension: `io.quarkus:quarkus-hibernate-orm`"
msgstr ""

msgid "your JDBC driver extension; the following options are available:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus-jdbc-db2` for link:https://www.ibm.com/products/db2-database[IBM "
"DB2]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus-jdbc-h2` for link:https://www.h2database.com/html/main.html[H2]"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jdbc-mariadb` for link:https://mariadb.com/[MariaDB]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus-jdbc-mssql` for link:https://www.microsoft.com/en-gb/sql-server/"
"[Microsoft SQL Server]"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus-jdbc-mysql` for link:https://www.mysql.com/[MySQL]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus-jdbc-oracle` for link:https://www.oracle.com/database/[Oracle "
"Database]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`quarkus-jdbc-postgresql` for link:https://www.postgresql.org/[PostgreSQL]"
msgstr ""

msgid "For instance:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Annotate your persistent objects with `@Entity`,\n"
"then add the relevant configuration properties in `{config-file}`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"xref:datasource.adoc[Configure the datasource] for production, relying on "
"xref:datasource#dev-services[Dev Services] for connection information in "
"tests / dev mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Configure Hibernate ORM to create the schema on startup in production, which "
"is useful for experimentation, but rely on <<dev-mode,convenient defaults in "
"tests / dev mode>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that configuration properties for the Hibernate ORM Quarkus extension "
"are not the same ones as in your typical Hibernate ORM configuration file.\n"
"They will often map to Hibernate ORM configuration properties but could have "
"different names and don't necessarily map 1:1 to each other."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Also, Quarkus will set many Hibernate ORM configuration settings "
"automatically, and will often use more modern defaults."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a list of the items that you can set in `{config-file}`, see "
"<<configuration-reference>>."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An `EntityManagerFactory` will be created based on the Quarkus `datasource` "
"configuration as long as the Hibernate ORM extension is listed among your "
"project dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The dialect will be selected and configured automatically based on your "
"datasource;\n"
"you may want to <<hibernate-dialect,configure it to more precisely match "
"your database>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can then happily inject your `EntityManager`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Inject your entity manager and have fun"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Mark your CDI bean method as `@Transactional` and the `EntityManager` will "
"enlist and flush at commit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To load SQL statements when Hibernate ORM starts, add an `import.sql` file "
"to the root of your `resources` directory.\n"
"This script can contain any SQL DML statements.\n"
"Make sure to terminate each statement with a semicolon."
msgstr ""

msgid "This is useful to have a data set ready for your tests or demos."
msgstr ""

msgid "Dialect"
msgstr ""

msgid "Supported databases"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For xref:datasource.adoc#extensions-and-database-drivers-reference[supported "
"databases],\n"
"the link:{hibernate-orm-docs-url}#database-dialect[Hibernate ORM dialect]\n"
"does not need to be set explicitly:\n"
"it is selected automatically based on the datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the dialect is configured to target the minimum supported "
"version of the database."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order for Hibernate ORM to generate more efficient SQL,\n"
"to avoid workarounds and to take advantage of more database features,\n"
"you can set the database version explicitly:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set the database version. The Hibernate ORM dialect will target that version."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As a rule, the version set here should be as high as possible,\n"
"but must be lower than or equal to the version of any database your "
"application will connect to."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As described above, the version can either be preconfigured explicitly via a "
"`quarkus.datasource.db-version` configuration property,\n"
"or implicitly set by the Quarkus build process to a minimum supported "
"version of the database.\n"
"Quarkus will try to check this preconfigured version against the actual "
"database version on startup,\n"
"leading to a startup failure when the actual version is lower."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This is a safeguard: for versions of the database older than what is "
"configured,\n"
"Hibernate ORM may generate SQL that is invalid which would lead to runtime "
"exceptions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the database cannot be reached, a warning will be logged but startup will "
"proceed.\n"
"If you know the database won't be reachable on startup, consider configuring "
"<<offline,offline startup>>,\n"
"which will automatically disable the check and warning."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As a last resort, you can disable the version check completely\n"
"using <<quarkus-hibernate-orm_quarkus-hibernate-orm-database-version-check-"
"enabled,`quarkus.hibernate-orm.database.version-check.enabled=false`>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Other databases"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If xref:datasource.adoc#other-databases[your database does not have a "
"corresponding Quarkus extension],\n"
"or if the defaults do not match your needs for some reason,\n"
"you will need to set the link:{hibernate-orm-docs-url}#database-"
"dialect[Hibernate ORM dialect] explicitly:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set the Hibernate ORM dialect."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For built-in dialects, the expected value is one of the names\n"
"in the link:{hibernate-orm-dialect-docs-url}[official list of dialects], "
"*without* the `Dialect` suffix,\n"
"for example `Cockroach` for `CockroachDialect`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For third-party dialects, the expected value is the fully-qualified class "
"name,\n"
"for example `com.acme.hibernate.AcmeDbDialect`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In that case, keep in mind that the JDBC driver or Hibernate ORM dialect\n"
"may not work properly in GraalVM native executables."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As with <<hibernate-dialect-supported-databases,supported databases>>,\n"
"you can configure the DB version explicitly to get the most out of Hibernate "
"ORM:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set the database version. The Hibernate ORM dialect will target that version."
"\n"
"Since we're targeting CockroachDB here, we're passing the CockroachDB "
"version, not the PostgreSQL version."
msgstr ""

msgid "Varying database"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When enabling <<database-approach,database multi-tenancy>>,\n"
"Hibernate ORM will use multiple datasources at runtime for the same "
"persistence unit,\n"
"and by default Quarkus cannot tell which datasource is going to be used,\n"
"so it will not be able to detect a dialect to use in Hibernate ORM."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For that reason, when enabling <<database-approach,database multi-tenancy>>,\n"
"it is recommended to explicitly point the Hibernate ORM configuration to one "
"datasource\n"
"among those that will be used at runtime, e.g. with `quarkus.hibernate-orm."
"datasource=base`\n"
"(`base` being the name of a datasource)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When doing so, Quarkus will infer the database version and (if possible) "
"dialect from that datasource.\n"
"For unsupported databases, you may still need to set the Hibernate ORM "
"dialect explicitly,\n"
"as explained in <<hibernate-dialect-other-databases,this section>>."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM configuration properties"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are various optional properties useful to refine your "
"`EntityManagerFactory` or guide guesses of Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are no required properties, as long as a default datasource is "
"configured."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When no property is set, Quarkus can typically infer everything it needs to "
"set up Hibernate ORM\n"
"and will have it use the default datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The configuration properties listed in <<configuration-reference>> allow you "
"to override such defaults, and customize and tune various aspects."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Do not mix <<persistence-xml,`persistence.xml`>> and `quarkus.hibernate-orm."
"*` properties in `{config-file}`.\n"
"Quarkus will raise an exception.\n"
"Make up your mind on which approach you want to use."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If your classpath contains a `persistence.xml` that you want to ignore,\n"
"set the following configuration property:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Multiple persistence units"
msgstr ""

msgid "Setting up multiple persistence units"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is possible to define multiple persistence units using the Quarkus "
"configuration properties."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The properties at the root of the `quarkus.hibernate-orm.` namespace define "
"the default persistence unit.\n"
"For instance, the following snippet defines a default datasource and a "
"default persistence unit:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using a map based approach, it is possible to define named persistence units:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid "Define a datasource named `users`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Define a datasource named `inventory`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Define a persistence unit called `users` pointing to the `users` datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This configuration property is important, but we will discuss it a bit later."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Define a persistence unit called `inventory` pointing to the `inventory` "
"datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can mix the default datasource and named datasources or only have one or "
"the other."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The default persistence unit points to the default datasource by default.\n"
"For named persistence units, the `datasource` property is mandatory.\n"
"You can point your persistence unit to the default datasource by setting it "
"to `<default>`\n"
"(which is the internal name of the default datasource)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is perfectly valid to have several persistence units pointing to the same "
"datasource."
msgstr ""

msgid "Attaching model classes to persistence units"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"There are two ways to attach model classes to persistence units, and they "
"should not be mixed:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Via the `packages` configuration property;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Via the `@io.quarkus.hibernate.orm.PersistenceUnit` package-level annotation."
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If both are mixed, the annotations are ignored and only the `packages` "
"configuration properties are taken into account."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using the `packages` configuration property is simple:"
msgstr ""

msgid "This configuration snippet will create two persistence units:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The default one which will contain all the model classes under the `org.acme."
"model.defaultpu` package, subpackages included."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A named `users` persistence unit which will contain all the model classes "
"under the `org.acme.model.user` package, subpackages included."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can attach several packages to a persistence unit:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the model classes under the `org.acme.model.shared` and `org.acme.model."
"user` packages will be attached to the `users` persistence unit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is also supported to attach a given model class to several persistence "
"units."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Model classes need to be consistently added to a given persistence unit.\n"
"That meant that all dependent model classes of a given entity (mapped super "
"classes, embeddables...) are required to be attached to the persistence unit."
"\n"
"As we are dealing with the persistence unit at the package level, it should "
"be simple enough."
msgstr ""

msgid "Panache entities can be attached to only one persistence unit."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For entities attached to several persistence units, you cannot use Panache.\n"
"You can mix the two approaches though and mix Panache entities and "
"traditional entities where multiple persistence units are required."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you have a use case for that and clever ideas about how to implement it "
"without cluttering the simplified Panache approach,\n"
"contact us on the link:{quarkus-mailing-list-index}[quarkus-dev mailing "
"list]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The second approach to attach model classes to a persistence unit is to use "
"package-level `@io.quarkus.hibernate.orm.PersistenceUnit` annotations.\n"
"Again, the two approaches cannot be mixed."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To obtain a configuration similar to the one above with the `packages` "
"configuration property, create a `package-info.java` file with the following "
"content:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be careful, use the `@io.quarkus.hibernate.orm.PersistenceUnit` annotation, "
"not the Jakarta Persistence one."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We only support defining the `@PersistenceUnit` for model classes at the "
"package level,\n"
"using the `@PersistenceUnit` annotation at the class level is not supported "
"in this case."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note that, similarly to what we do with the configuration property, we take "
"into account the annotated package but also all its subpackages."
msgstr ""

